target:
def Target : Prop :=
  ∀ (F : ArithmeticTheory) [F.Δ₁] [𝗜𝚺₁ ⪯ F],
    F ⊢ (F.consistent.val 🡒 gödel F.standardProvability)

b_raw:
{
  "verdict": "faithful_with_caveats",
  "divergences": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chalmers considers a sound F that might capture our reasoning. Lean assumes neither soundness nor any connection to human reasoning. This harmlessly strengthens item (b): it is the conditional that F proves, even when F is unsound."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean makes a specific choice of scope where the passage says only “formal system”: F must be an arithmetic theory with a Δ₁ axiom presentation that proves every theorem of IΣ₁. The target does not directly cover other presentations or weaker base theories."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean reads “G(F) is true” disquotationally: the consequent is the Gödel sentence itself, not a separate assertion of standard-model truth. This is the usual reading for a fixed arithmetic sentence."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The target preserves the key scope and direction of item (b): F proves the implication from its arithmetized consistency to its Gödel sentence. It does not say that F proves either sentence separately."
}
